{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff c6187d68 25a908fb --stat && cat collab/1792360000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md && cat collab/m012d-report.log'","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-RGOKer3Y' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-18 02:14:32.924 xcodebuild[16912:71573917]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-18 02:14:33.250 xcodebuild[16912:71573909] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-GXz4PXT3' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n2026-10-18 02:14:33.879 xcodebuild[16917:71573952]  DVTFilePathFSEvents: Failed to start fs event stream.\n2026-10-18 02:14:34.066 xcodebuild[16917:71573951] [MT] DVTDeveloperPaths: Failed to get length of DARWIN_USER_CACHE_DIR from confstr(3), error = Error Domain=NSPOSIXErrorDomain Code=5 \"Input/output error\". Using NSCachesDirectory instead.\n docs/design/yang.antlr.md                   |  23 +-\n src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc             |  58 +++--\n src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc             | 356 ++++++++++++++++++++++------\n test/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc            | 123 +++++++++-\n test/yang/python/antlr/cst_export_test.cljc | 105 +++++---\n test/yin/repl/python_antlr_test.cljc        |   4 +-\n 6 files changed, 541 insertions(+), 128 deletions(-)\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-17 18:05:52 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-18 01:05:52 +07 (+0700)\nCoding-Agent: codex gpt-6.1-sol\n\n(exported from the JSONL stdout log by the orchestrator; probe transcripts live in the log)\n\nRead-only probes confirmed that the validator and oracle accept duplicate child edges, wrong token text, a collapsed synthetic NAME, and a span ending inside `é`. These are cases the approved contract requires them to reject.\n\nThe build pins and three-host wiring look consistent. The merge also restores master’s scanner pins and log entries; the prelude diff plausibly preserves JVM/Node data as reported. The three JS compatibility additions are recorded in the manifest/code and report, but not in the design document.\n\n\nCompleted-GMT: 2026-10-17 18:05:52 GMT\nCompleted-Local: 2026-10-18 01:05:52 +07 (+0700)\n\nM0 and the three-host parser wiring largely match the plan. M1 does not implement the strengthened contract on which v3 received sign-off.\n\n1. **P1 — The promised validator remains unimplemented.** [packet.cljc:150](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-antlr-multi/src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc:150) checks forward edges and reachability, but permits duplicate siblings and non-DFS child ordering. [conform:219](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-antlr-multi/src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc:219) omits source-text equality, UTF-8 boundary alignment, grammar-name validation, and outcome-specific contracts. Read-only JVM probes confirmed both checks accept duplicate edges, wrong text/rule names, and spans ending inside `é`; a separate probe confirmed non-DFS ordering also passes. Implement §4.6’s validator and rejection cases before landing.\n\n2. **P1 — Synthetic-token handling repeats the rejected policy.** [export.cljc:55](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-antlr-multi/src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc:55) marks any text mismatch or overlap synthetic and preserves runtime text. There is no type-keyed `:synthetic-policy` or canonical helper text. A collapsed synthetic NAME passes validation and conformance. Implement the approved DEDENT/NEWLINE/EOF policy and canonical text while retaining independent exporter evidence.\n\n3. **P1 — The required adversarial conformance corpus is missing.** [conformance.cljc:12](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-antlr-multi/test/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc:12) drops child edges and synthetic flags from its comparison shape; its error helper never checks columns. The exporter tests lack the twelve required mutations and the two pinned helper-token error-coordinate disagreements. The `[4 99]` mutation proves Dart executes that span assertion; it does not establish the approved oracle. Add the complete acceptance/mutation corpus on all three hosts.\n\n4. **P2 — Record the compatibility additions in the design hub.** Duplicate-method removal, generated JS import rewriting, and the runtime default fallback are narrow, justified fixes, with exact patches and digests recorded in the manifest. They are declared in the report, but absent from `yang.antlr.md`. Document them there as requested.\n\nThe remaining gate questions do not add blockers:\n\n- Vendored grammar inputs, Java digest preservation, runtime pins, frontend revision `f4`, and the host-neutral parser/export split are consistent with scope. The `é𝄞` conversion path and fixture are plausible and supported by the supplied lane evidence.\n- JS/Dart workers allocate fresh DFA entries and prediction-context caches and install their own simulators. I accept the explicitly recorded isolation-test debt as nonblocking.\n- The prelude diff changes quoted-data construction without changing its payload. JVM/Node expand to plain definitions in the verified builds, making the unchanged scanner and linker pins plausible.\n- Helper licensing remains unresolved and generated-artifact redistribution remains blocked; the landing does not grant broader redistribution.\n- The merge restores master’s scanner pins and log entries. I found no additional legacy-frontend or linker regression in the reviewed diff.\n\nReview was read-only. Supplied verification lanes were not rerun; only focused validator probes were executed.\n\nVerdict: REQUEST CHANGESAll four findings are resolved and committed on `antlr-multi` as `25a908fb`. I did not push, did not touch master, and `collab/` stays untracked. The JVM, Node and Dart quick lanes pass. Kondo reports 0 errors and 0 warnings on the changed files, and `cljstyle check` printed nothing.\n\n## Resolution map\n\n**P1-1, validator.**\n- **`packet.cljc`:** `validate!` and `conform` now share one `violations` function. `validate!` is structural by default and source-aware with `{:source …}`. `conform [packet source opts]` is source-aware and also accepts `:rule-names`.\n- **Structural checks:** a single preorder walk rejects duplicate edges, out-of-order children, non-forward edges and unreachable nodes. Metadata checks cover version, unit, grammar name and completion. Outcome contracts distinguish ok packets from error packets, and error records are checked for kind, message, line, column and span.\n- **Source checks:** token text must equal the source, and spans must be in range and on UTF-8 boundaries. Terminals must be in order, rule extents must cover real children, and synthetic tokens must follow the policy.\n\n**P1-2, synthetic policy.**\n- **Policy:** `packet/synthetic-policy` is keyed on token type. DEDENT and EOF are always synthetic, NEWLINE only at the end of the source, and every other type never.\n- **Exporter:** `export.cljc` decides by type. A NEWLINE is synthetic only when the source disagrees with the helper and it sits at the end. Synthetic tokens get canonical text and a zero-width span.\n- **Result:** a collapsed synthetic NAME now fails validation and conform.\n- **Canonical text:** I chose DEDENT `\"\"`, NEWLINE `\"\\n\"` and EOF `\"<EOF>\"`. The helper's own text varied, for example `\"y = 1\"` and `\"  # c\"` on EOF.\n\n**P1-3, corpus.**\n- **`conformance.cljc`:** `shape` now includes child edges and synthetic flags. `check-error` checks columns and validates the error packet.\n- **Mutations:** `check-mutations` runs 14 mutations, which are your twelve plus two extras, a real EOF and a mid-file synthetic NEWLINE. Each must be refused by both `validate!` and `conform`, and the unmutated packet must conform. It runs on `\"s = 'é𝄞'\\nt = 2\\n\"`.\n- **Error-coordinate pins:** two helper-token disagreements are pinned, using the source `\"  x = 1\\n\"`.\n- **Golden:** the golden test now asserts children and synthetic flags.\n- **`python_antlr_test`:** it used to run `conform` on hand-built packets with zero spans, which the strict oracle now rejects. It now conforms the parser's packet and still compares node shapes.\n\n**P2, design doc.** §4.6 now documents the duplicate `getIndentationCount` removal, the `:output-patches` import rewrite and the antlr4-default fallback, with manifest and file pointers and no collab references. It also notes that helper-token error coordinates are pinned per host.\n\n## Tests\n\n| Host | Result |\n|---|---|\n| JVM | `cst-export-test` went from 12 tests / 52 assertions to 15 / 151. The `python-antlr`, `lower-portable` and `scope` namespaces also pass. |\n| Node | No failures. The log prints no counts, but \"Testing yang.python.antlr.cst-export-test\" appears. |\n| Dart | `+4025: All tests passed!`. |\n\nThe `[4 99]` span probe was already in the earlier Dart run. The 14-mutation corpus now runs in all three lanes.\n\n## Probe cases now refused\n\nAll four are covered by the mutation corpus above:\n- Duplicate child edges.\n- Wrong token text.\n- A collapsed synthetic NAME.\n- A span ending inside `é`.\n\nNon-DFS child ordering is refused too, through the \"children out of preorder\" mutation.\n\n## Finding to review\n\nThe helper-token error coordinates differ by host, which I did not expect. I pinned them per host instead of asserting one value:\n\n| Error | JVM | Node | Dart |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| INDENT error column | 2 | 2 | 0 |\n| EOF error [line column] | [1 0] | [2 0] | [1 7] |\n\nThe byte spans agree on all three hosts. This matches §4.6's \"not required to agree\", but it means the Node and Dart helpers differ from the JVM's. You may want that recorded as known debt.\n\n## Left open\n\n- The token-ordering check requires a synthetic token to start at or after the previous real token's end. It held on every fixture here, but I have not tried it against more sources.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
