{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat test/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc; cat test/yang/python/antlr/cst_export_test.cljc; cat src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc; cat collab/1792304000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-plan-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md'","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.antlr.conformance\n  \"The per-target, language-free exporter oracle (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n   §5.5): a language's fixtures are run against the exporter of the running\n   host, JVM, Node or Dart, and every one must come out the same. A fixture is\n   a source string and either its expected `shape` or the error it must\n   produce. The goldens are the JVM's; they are the cross-target oracle.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [is testing]]\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as packet]))\n\n\n(defn shape\n  \"A packet's nodes in preorder: [rule span children] for a rule and\n   [type text span synthetic?] for a token. The child edges and the synthetic\n   flags are part of the shape, so a tree that differs only in them differs.\"\n  [pk]\n  (mapv (fn [n]\n          (if (= :rule (:kind n))\n            [(:rule n) (:span n) (:children n)]\n            [(:type n) (:text n) (:span n) (boolean (:synthetic n))]))\n        (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))\n\n\n(defn check-ok\n  \"`source` parses to an ok packet that validates and conforms (invariants\n   1-5); with `expected` the packet's shape equals it. Returns the packet.\"\n  ([parse source] (check-ok parse source nil))\n  ([parse source expected]\n   (let [pk (parse source)]\n     (is (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk)) source)\n     (is (some? (packet/validate! pk {:source source})) source)\n     (is (= [] (packet/conform pk source)) source)\n     (when expected\n       (is (= expected (shape pk)) source))\n     pk)))\n\n\n(defn check-error\n  \"`source` yields a syntax-error packet with no nodes that validates and\n   whose first error has the given `line`, `column` and `span` (invariant 6).\n   ANTLR's line and column and the byte span are independent coordinates, so\n   each is pinned on its own. Returns the packet.\"\n  [parse source {:keys [line column span]}]\n  (let [pk (parse source)\n        e (first (:yang.cst/errors pk))]\n    (testing source\n      (is (= :yang.cst/syntax-error (:yang.cst/outcome pk)))\n      (is (not (contains? pk :yang.cst/nodes)) \"never a partial program\")\n      (is (not (contains? pk :yang.cst/root)))\n      (is (true? (:yang.cst/complete pk)))\n      (is (= :syntax-error (:kind e)))\n      (is (string? (:message e)))\n      (is (some? (packet/validate! pk {:source source})))\n      (is (= [] (packet/conform pk source)))\n      (when line (is (= line (:line e))))\n      (when column (is (= column (:column e))))\n      (when span (is (= span (:span e)))))\n    pk))\n\n\n(defn check-fixtures\n  \"Run each fixture {:source s :shape [...]} or {:source s :error {...}}.\"\n  [parse fixtures]\n  (doseq [{:keys [source shape error]} fixtures]\n    (if error\n      (check-error parse source error)\n      (check-ok parse source shape))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The adversarial corpus: packets that must be rejected\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- first-node\n  [pk pred]\n  (first (filter pred (:yang.cst/nodes pk))))\n\n\n(defn- token-of\n  [pk type]\n  (first-node pk #(and (= :token (:kind %)) (= type (:type %)))))\n\n\n(defn- edit\n  [pk id f]\n  (update-in pk [:yang.cst/nodes id] f))\n\n\n(def mutations\n  \"Named mutations of a good packet for a source with a multi-byte string\n   token; each yields a packet `validate!` and `conform` must refuse. Pair\n   with `check-mutations`.\"\n  [[\"duplicate child edge\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [r (first-node pk #(and (= :rule (:kind %)) (seq (:children %))))]\n        (edit pk (:id r) #(update % :children (fn [k] (into [(first k)] k))))))]\n   [\"wrong token text\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk (:id (token-of pk \"NAME\")) #(assoc % :text \"wrong\")))]\n   [\"collapsed synthetic NAME\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"NAME\")\n            a (first (:span t))]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :synthetic true, :text \"\", :span [a a]))))]\n   [\"span ending inside a multi-byte character\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (first-node pk #(and (= :token (:kind %))\n                                   (= \"STRING\" (:type %))))\n            a (first (:span t))]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :span [a (+ a 2)]))))]\n   [\"children out of preorder\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [r (first-node pk #(and (= :rule (:kind %))\n                                   (< 1 (count (:children %)))))]\n        (edit pk (:id r) #(update % :children (comp vec reverse)))))]\n   [\"node unreachable from the root\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [end (count (:yang.cst/nodes pk))]\n        (update pk :yang.cst/nodes conj\n                {:id end, :kind :token, :type \"NAME\", :text \"\", :span [0 0]})))]\n   [\"span past the end of the source\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk (:id (token-of pk \"NAME\")) #(assoc % :span [0 99])))]\n   [\"blank grammar name\" (fn [pk] (assoc pk :yang.cst/grammar \"\"))]\n   [\"rule name outside the grammar\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk 0 #(assoc % :rule \"no_such_rule\")))]\n   [\"real token overlapping the previous one\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"ASSIGN\")]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :span [0 (second (:span %))]))))]\n   [\"rule span not covering its children\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk 0 #(assoc % :span [0 1])))]\n   [\"error packet that still carries nodes\"\n    (fn [pk] (assoc pk :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/syntax-error))]\n   [\"EOF presented as real source\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"EOF\")]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(dissoc % :synthetic))))]\n   [\"synthetic NEWLINE in the middle of the source\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"NEWLINE\")\n            a (first (:span t))]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :synthetic true, :span [a a]))))]])\n\n\n(defn- refused?\n  [pk opts]\n  (try (packet/validate! pk opts)\n       false\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                 :clj clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo\n                 :cljs ExceptionInfo)\n              _\n         true)))\n\n\n(defn check-mutations\n  \"`source` parses to a packet that conforms; every mutation of it is then\n   refused by both `validate!` (with the source) and `conform`.\"\n  [parse source]\n  (let [pk (parse source)\n        opts {:source source,\n              :rule-names (set (keep :rule (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))}]\n    (is (= [] (packet/violations pk opts)) \"the unmutated packet conforms\")\n    (doseq [[label f] mutations\n            :let [m (f pk)]]\n      (testing label\n        (is (not= pk m) \"the mutation changed the packet\")\n        (is (seq (packet/violations m opts)))\n        (is (seq (packet/conform m source (select-keys opts [:rule-names]))))\n        (is (refused? m opts))))))\n(ns yang.python.antlr.cst-export-test\n  \"The parser interpreter on every host: CST packet goldens (rule names, byte\n   spans, synthetic tokens) through the language-free conformance oracle,\n   syntax errors as records with no nodes, the source protocol, and chunk\n   invariance.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n    [dao.stream :as stream]\n    [yang.antlr.conformance :as conformance :refer [shape]]\n    [yang.antlr.cst :as cst]\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as packet]\n    [yang.python.antlr.parser :as parser]\n    [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n\n\n(deftest golden-assignment-test\n  (let [pk (parser/parse-source \"x = 1\\n\")]\n    (conformance/check-ok parser/parse-source \"x = 1\\n\")\n    (is (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk)))\n    (is (= parser/grammar-id (:yang.cst/grammar pk)))\n    (is (true? (:yang.cst/complete pk)))\n    (is (= 0 (:yang.cst/root pk)))\n    (is (= [[\"file_input\" [0 6] [1 28]]\n            [\"stmt\" [0 6] [2]]\n            [\"simple_stmts\" [0 6] [3 27]]\n            [\"simple_stmt\" [0 5] [4]]\n            [\"expr_stmt\" [0 5] [5 16 17]]\n            [\"testlist_star_expr\" [0 1] [6]]\n            [\"test\" [0 1] [7]]\n            [\"or_test\" [0 1] [8]]\n            [\"and_test\" [0 1] [9]]\n            [\"not_test\" [0 1] [10]]\n            [\"comparison\" [0 1] [11]]\n            [\"expr\" [0 1] [12]]\n            [\"atom_expr\" [0 1] [13]]\n            [\"atom\" [0 1] [14]]\n            [\"name\" [0 1] [15]]\n            [\"NAME\" \"x\" [0 1] false]\n            [\"ASSIGN\" \"=\" [2 3] false]\n            [\"testlist_star_expr\" [4 5] [18]]\n            [\"test\" [4 5] [19]]\n            [\"or_test\" [4 5] [20]]\n            [\"and_test\" [4 5] [21]]\n            [\"not_test\" [4 5] [22]]\n            [\"comparison\" [4 5] [23]]\n            [\"expr\" [4 5] [24]]\n            [\"atom_expr\" [4 5] [25]]\n            [\"atom\" [4 5] [26]]\n            [\"NUMBER\" \"1\" [4 5] false]\n            [\"NEWLINE\" \"\\n\" [5 6] false]\n            [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\" [6 6] true]]\n           (shape pk)))\n    (testing \"ids are preorder indexes and children are ordered edges\"\n      (is (= (range (count (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))\n             (map :id (:yang.cst/nodes pk))))\n      (is (= [5 16 17] (:children (packet/node pk 4))))\n      (is (some? (packet/validate! pk))))\n    (testing \"EOF is synthetic and zero-width\"\n      (is (:synthetic (peek (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))))))\n\n\n(deftest spans-are-utf8-bytes-test\n  (testing \"a two-byte and a four-byte code point before a token shift its\n            span by bytes, not characters\"\n    (let [src \"s = 'é𝄞'\\nt = 2\\n\"\n          pk (parser/parse-source src)\n          tok (fn [text] (first (filter #(= text (:text %)) (:yang.cst/nodes pk))))]\n      (conformance/check-ok parser/parse-source src)\n      (is (= [4 12] (:span (tok \"'é𝄞'\"))))\n      (is (= [13 14] (:span (tok \"t\"))))\n      (is (= (cst/utf8-bytes src) (second (:span (packet/root pk))))))))\n\n\n(deftest indentation-tokens-test\n  (let [pk (parser/parse-source \"if x:\\n    y = 1\\nz = 2\\n\")\n        toks (filterv #(= :token (:kind %)) (:yang.cst/nodes pk))\n        by-type (fn [t] (filterv #(= t (:type %)) toks))]\n    (testing \"INDENT covers the indentation it stands for\"\n      (is (= [[\"    \" [6 10] nil]]\n             (mapv (juxt :text :span :synthetic) (by-type \"INDENT\")))))\n    (testing \"DEDENT is synthetic and zero-width where the dedented line\n              starts (patched helper)\"\n      (let [[d] (by-type \"DEDENT\")]\n        (is (:synthetic d))\n        (is (= [16 16] (:span d)))))\n    (testing \"every NEWLINE sits on its newline, including the one before an\n              INDENT (patched helper)\"\n      (is (= [[nil [5 6]] [nil [15 16]] [nil [21 22]]]\n             (mapv (juxt :synthetic :span) (by-type \"NEWLINE\")))))\n    (testing \"a block's span covers its real text only\"\n      (let [block (first (filter #(= \"block\" (:rule %)) (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))]\n        (is (= [5 16] (:span block)))))))\n\n\n(deftest missing-final-newline-test\n  (testing \"known limitation of the pinned grammar's Java helper: it adds an\n            end-of-input NEWLINE only while indentation is open, so a\n            top-level statement without a final newline is a syntax error\n            record; the source is not silently normalized\"\n    (let [pk (parser/parse-source \"x = 1\")]\n      (is (= :yang.cst/syntax-error (:yang.cst/outcome pk))))\n    (let [pk (parser/parse-source \"if x:\\n    y = 1\")\n          nl (last (filter #(= \"NEWLINE\" (:type %)) (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))]\n      (is (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk)))\n      (is (:synthetic nl))\n      (is (= [15 15] (:span nl))))))\n\n\n(deftest syntax-errors-are-records-test\n  (let [pk (parser/parse-source \"def f(:\\n    return 1\\n\")]\n    (is (= :yang.cst/syntax-error (:yang.cst/outcome pk)))\n    (is (not (contains? pk :yang.cst/nodes)) \"never a partial program\")\n    (is (not (contains? pk :yang.cst/root)))\n    (is (true? (:yang.cst/complete pk)))\n    (let [[e :as errors] (:yang.cst/errors pk)]\n      (is (seq errors))\n      (is (= :syntax-error (:kind e)))\n      (is (= 1 (:line e)))\n      (is (= 6 (:column e)))\n      (is (= [6 7] (:span e)))\n      (is (string? (:message e))))))\n\n\n(deftest lexer-errors-are-records-test\n  (conformance/check-error parser/parse-source \"x = $\\n\"\n                           {:line 1, :column 4, :span [4 5]}))\n\n\n(deftest error-coordinates-are-independent-test\n  (testing \"the byte span comes from the token indexes and ANTLR's line and\n            column are captured as reported: they need not agree. The\n            indentation helper places an unexpected INDENT's column after the\n            indentation (the span starts at 0), and its EOF token reports a\n            line and column of its own while the span is the end of the\n            source. These coordinates are each target helper's own, pinned\n            per host: the INDENT column is 2 on the JVM and Node and 0 on\n            Dart; the EOF [line column] is [1 0] on the JVM, [2 0] on Node\n            and [1 7] on Dart.\"\n    (let [pk (conformance/check-error parser/parse-source \"  x = 1\\n\"\n                                      {:line 1,\n                                       :column #?(:cljd 0 :default 2),\n                                       :span [0 2]})\n          e (second (:yang.cst/errors pk))]\n      (is (= [#?(:cljs 2 :default 1) #?(:cljd 7 :default 0) [8 8]]\n             ((juxt :line :column :span) e)))))\n  (testing \"where they do agree they are still both recorded\"\n    (conformance/check-error parser/parse-source \"if x:\\npass\\n\"\n                             {:line 2, :column 0, :span [6 10]})))\n\n\n(deftest packets-keep-the-synthetic-policy-test\n  (testing \"helper tokens carry their type's canonical text\"\n    (let [pk (parser/parse-source \"if x:\\n    y = 1\\nz = 2\\n\")\n          dedent (first (filter #(= \"DEDENT\" (:type %)) (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))]\n      (conformance/check-ok parser/parse-source \"if x:\\n    y = 1\\nz = 2\\n\")\n      (is (= [\"\" [16 16] true] ((juxt :text :span :synthetic) dedent)))))\n  (testing \"a comment before the end of input leaves the helpers at the end\"\n    (let [src \"if x:\\n    y = 1  # c\"\n          pk (conformance/check-ok parser/parse-source src)\n          helpers (filterv :synthetic (:yang.cst/nodes pk))]\n      (is (= [[\"NEWLINE\" \"\\n\"] [\"DEDENT\" \"\"] [\"EOF\" \"<EOF>\"]]\n             (mapv (juxt :type :text) helpers)))\n      (is (every? #(= [20 20] (:span %)) helpers)))))\n\n\n(deftest adversarial-mutations-are-refused-test\n  (conformance/check-mutations parser/parse-source \"s = 'é𝄞'\\nt = 2\\n\"))\n\n\n(deftest exporter-is-deterministic-test\n  (let [src \"def f(a):\\n    return [a, {1: 'x'}]\\n\"]\n    (is (= (parser/parse-source src)\n           (parser/parse-source (parser/make-worker) [:unit 0] src)))))\n\n\n(deftest every-grammar-rule-name-is-exported-by-name-test\n  (testing \"rule records use the grammar's rule names\"\n    (let [names (set parser/rule-names)\n          pk (parser/parse-source\n               \"class A(B):\\n    def m(self, *a):\\n        while x: pass\\n\")]\n      (is (every? #(contains? names (:rule %))\n                  (filter #(= :rule (:kind %)) (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The stage: source events in, packets out\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- chunks\n  \"Split `src` at the given character offsets.\"\n  [src cuts]\n  (let [bounds (concat [0] cuts [(count src)])]\n    (mapv (fn [[a b]] (subs src a b)) (partition 2 1 bounds))))\n\n\n(defn- source-events\n  [unit texts]\n  (conj (vec (map-indexed (fn [i t]\n                            {:yang.source/event :yang.source/chunk,\n                             :yang.source/unit unit,\n                             :yang.source/ordinal i,\n                             :yang.source/text t})\n                          texts))\n        {:yang.source/event :yang.source/seal,\n         :yang.source/unit unit,\n         :yang.source/chunk-count (count texts)}))\n\n\n(defn- run-parser\n  [events]\n  (let [src (tu/new-memory-log)\n        out (tu/new-memory-log)]\n    (doseq [e events] (stream/append! src e))\n    (let [s (parser/step-stage (parser/open-stage src out))]\n      {:stage s, :packets (tu/drain out)})))\n\n\n(deftest stage-emits-one-packet-per-sealed-unit-test\n  (let [{:keys [stage packets]}\n        (run-parser (concat (source-events [:u 1] [\"x = 1\\n\"])\n                            (source-events [:u 2] [\"def f(:\\n\"])))]\n    (is (= :blocked (:status stage)))\n    (is (= [[:u 1] [:u 2]] (mapv :yang.cst/unit packets)))\n    (is (= [:yang.cst/ok :yang.cst/syntax-error]\n           (mapv :yang.cst/outcome packets)))\n    (is (= {} (:state stage)) \"sealed units leave no state behind\")))\n\n\n(deftest stage-waits-for-the-seal-test\n  (let [{:keys [stage packets]}\n        (run-parser (butlast (source-events [:u 1] [\"x = 1\\n\"])))]\n    (is (empty? packets))\n    (is (= {[:u 1] {0 \"x = 1\\n\"}} (:state stage)))))\n\n\n(deftest source-protocol-errors-test\n  (testing \"a seal with a missing chunk\"\n    (let [[chunk0 _chunk1 seal] (source-events [:u 1] [\"x = \" \"1\\n\"])\n          {:keys [packets]} (run-parser [chunk0 seal])]\n      (is (= :yang.cst/source-error (:yang.cst/outcome (first packets))))\n      (is (not (contains? (first packets) :yang.cst/nodes)))))\n  (testing \"a conflicting duplicate chunk\"\n    (let [[chunk0 _ seal] (source-events [:u 1] [\"x = \" \"1\\n\"])\n          {:keys [packets]}\n          (run-parser [chunk0 (assoc chunk0 :yang.source/text \"y = \") seal])]\n      (is (= :yang.cst/source-error (:yang.cst/outcome (first packets)))))))\n\n\n(deftest chunk-invariance-test\n  (let [src \"def f(a):\\n    s = 'é'\\n    return a\\nprint(f(1))\\n\"\n        splits [[] [1] [5 6 7] [10 11 12 13] (vec (range 1 (count src)))]\n        packets (mapv (fn [cuts]\n                        (first (:packets (run-parser\n                                           (source-events [:u 1]\n                                                          (chunks src cuts))))))\n                      splits)]\n    (is (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome (first packets))))\n    (is (apply = packets))\n    (is (= (first packets) (parser/parse-source (parser/make-worker) [:u 1] src)))))\n(ns yang.antlr.export\n  \"The host-free half of a CST exporter (docs/design/yang.antlr.md §5.5): the\n   byte-offset table, the token and rule records, the synthetic-token rule\n   and the error record. A host's `yang.antlr.cst` walks its own parse-tree\n   objects through a small `ops` map and gets back the portable nodes:\n\n     {:token?    (fn [node] bool)           ; a terminal node\n      :token     (fn [node] {:type-name s :start i :stop i :text s})\n      :rule-name (fn [ctx] string)\n      :children  (fn [ctx] vector)\n      :start     (fn [ctx] start-index or nil)}\n\n   Indexes are code-point indexes into the source, the unit all three\n   targets use.\"\n  (:require\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as packet]))\n\n\n(defn byte-offsets\n  \"Byte offset of each code point index of `cps`, plus the total at index n.\"\n  [cps]\n  (packet/byte-offsets cps))\n\n\n(defn offset-at\n  [offsets i]\n  (nth offsets (max 0 (min i (dec (count offsets))))))\n\n\n(defn token-span\n  \"The byte span of a token's code point range [start, stop]; a token whose\n   stop precedes its start is zero-width.\"\n  [offsets start stop]\n  (let [s (offset-at offsets start)]\n    [s (if (< stop start) s (offset-at offsets (inc stop)))]))\n\n\n(defn syntax-error\n  [message line column span]\n  {:kind :syntax-error, :message (str message), :line line, :column column,\n   :span span})\n\n\n(defn- synthetic-token?\n  \"Whether a token is synthetic, decided on its type by\n   `packet/synthetic-policy`. DEDENT and EOF always are. A NEWLINE is only\n   when the source disagrees with the helper (its text is not the source at\n   its range, or its range overlaps the previous real token) and it sits at\n   the end of the source; every other type is never synthetic, so a token\n   the policy forbids stays real and the validator rejects its text.\"\n  [cps offsets last-stop {:keys [type-name start stop text]}]\n  (let [n (dec (count offsets))\n        policy (get packet/synthetic-policy type-name)]\n    (case (:when policy)\n      :always true\n      :at-end (and (or (not= (when (and (<= 0 start) (<= start stop) (< stop n))\n                               (subvec cps start (inc stop)))\n                             (some-> text packet/code-points))\n                       (<= start last-stop))\n                   (>= stop (dec n)))\n      false)))\n\n\n(defn- token-record\n  \"`last-stop` is the stop index of the previous real token: a NEWLINE that\n   overlaps it was produced by a helper, not read from the source. A\n   synthetic token is zero-width and carries its type's canonical text.\"\n  [cps offsets last-stop id {:keys [type-name start stop text], :as tok}]\n  (if (synthetic-token? cps offsets last-stop tok)\n    (let [p (offset-at offsets (inc stop))]\n      {:id id,\n       :kind :token,\n       :type type-name,\n       :text (get-in packet/synthetic-policy [type-name :text] text),\n       :span [p p],\n       :synthetic true})\n    {:id id,\n     :kind :token,\n     :type type-name,\n     :text text,\n     :span [(offset-at offsets start) (offset-at offsets (inc stop))]}))\n\n\n(defn export-nodes\n  \"Preorder records for the parse tree under `root`; a record's id is its\n   index.\"\n  [ops cps offsets root]\n  (let [out (volatile! [])\n        last-stop (volatile! -1)]\n    (letfn [(walk\n              [t]\n              (let [id (count @out)]\n                (if ((:token? ops) t)\n                  (let [tok ((:token ops) t)\n                        record (token-record cps offsets @last-stop id tok)]\n                    (when-not (:synthetic record)\n                      (vreset! last-stop (:stop tok)))\n                    (vswap! out conj record))\n                  (do\n                    (vswap! out conj nil)\n                    (let [kids (mapv walk ((:children ops) t))\n                          records @out\n                          ;; a rule covers its real text: synthetic tokens\n                          ;; and empty rules do not stretch it\n                          child-spans (keep (fn [k]\n                                              (let [r (nth records k)\n                                                    [a b] (:span r)]\n                                                (when (and (not (:synthetic r))\n                                                           (< a b))\n                                                  [a b])))\n                                            kids)\n                          start ((:start ops) t)\n                          s (if start (offset-at offsets start) 0)\n                          span (if (seq child-spans)\n                                 [(apply min (map first child-spans))\n                                  (apply max (map second child-spans))]\n                                 [s s])]\n                      (vswap! out assoc id\n                              {:id id,\n                               :kind :rule,\n                               :rule ((:rule-name ops) t),\n                               :children kids,\n                               :span span}))))\n                id))]\n      (walk root)\n      @out)))\n\n\n(defn result\n  \"The packet for a parse: an error packet when `errors` is non-empty.\"\n  [profile unit errors nodes]\n  (let [base (packet/base (:grammar-id profile) unit)]\n    (if (seq errors)\n      (assoc base\n             :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/syntax-error\n             :yang.cst/errors errors)\n      (assoc base\n             :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/ok\n             :yang.cst/root 0\n             :yang.cst/nodes (nodes)))))\n\n\n(defn failure-kind\n  \"Classify a parse's first failure. `failure` is nil (the parse had none),\n   :lexical (a lexer error, which has no token), or the index of the failing\n   token; `real-tokens` are the buffered non-EOF tokens as\n   {:index :start :stop}. End-of-input tokens are EOF and the zero-width ones\n   after the last token with source text (the lexer's EOF can carry a span,\n   so it is excluded by type). Only a failure there is mendable by more\n   input: :end; any earlier failure is :early.\"\n  [failure real-tokens]\n  (let [last-real (reduce max -1\n                          (keep (fn [{:keys [index start stop]}]\n                                  (when (<= start stop) index))\n                                real-tokens))]\n    (cond\n      (nil? failure) nil\n      (and (integer? failure) (> failure last-real)) :end\n      :else :early)))\nI’ll read the v3 corrections, trace them back to the prior findings, and check that the synthetic-token and coordinate rules resolve both P1s.\n\n\nThe revised policy accepts the zero-width DEDENT and rejects a collapsed NAME by type. The error contract also explicitly permits listener coordinates to disagree with the source span, and both helper-token error cases are pinned in the corpus. I’m checking the mutation table and retained exporter for inconsistencies.\n\n\nThe JVM probes match all three acceptance cases and both helper-token error fixtures. The v2-to-v3 diff preserves the preorder, text, UTF-8 boundary, ordering, extent, build, isolation, and retirement requirements. I found no remaining architectural blocker; implementation still has to pass M1 on all three hosts.\n\n\nCompleted-GMT / Completed-Local\n2026-10-17 13:20:24 GMT / 2026-10-17 20:20:24 +0700\n\nNo blocking findings. Both P1 corrections are resolved at the design level.\n\n- **Synthetic tokens:** the type-keyed policy accepts DEDENT `{:text \"\" :span [16 16] :synthetic true}` and rejects collapsed NAME tokens. Exporter evidence remains independent; canonical text removes runtime fallback text from packets. Three acceptance fixtures and twelve mutations are required on every host.\n- **Error coordinates:** source spans and verbatim ANTLR coordinates have separate invariants. JVM probes confirmed NEWLINE `{:line 3 :column 0 :span [13 14]}` and DEDENT `{:line 3 :column 0 :span [26 26]}`; both disagreements are pinned as expected values.\n- **Preservation:** ledger rows 10/11 address the findings. Preorder, uniqueness, real-token text, UTF-8 boundaries, terminal ordering, and rule extents remain enforced. No architectural regression found in the delta.\n\nReview was read-only. Existing JVM probes passed; proposed validators and JS/Dart parity remain M1 implementation gates.\n\nVerdict: READY (sign-off granted)","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc; sed -n '400,470p' src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc; rg -n 'mutation|NEWLINE|DEDENT|independent|synthetic-policy|disagree|twelve|twelve|error-coordinate' docs/design/yang.antlr.md collab/*antlr* | head -160; sed -n '1,65p' deps.edn; command -v bb; command -v clojure\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat test/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc; sed -n '400,470p' src/cljc/yang/antlr/packet.cljc; rg -n 'mutation|NEWLINE|DEDENT|independent|synthetic-policy|disagree|twelve|twelve|error-coordinate' docs/design/yang.antlr.md collab/*antlr* | head -160; sed -n '1,65p' deps.edn; command -v bb; command -v clojure\"","aggregated_output":"(ns yang.antlr.conformance\n  \"The per-target, language-free exporter oracle (docs/design/yang.antlr.md\n   §5.5): a language's fixtures are run against the exporter of the running\n   host, JVM, Node or Dart, and every one must come out the same. A fixture is\n   a source string and either its expected `shape` or the error it must\n   produce. The goldens are the JVM's; they are the cross-target oracle.\"\n  (:require\n    [clojure.test :refer [is testing]]\n    [yang.antlr.packet :as packet]))\n\n\n(defn shape\n  \"A packet's nodes in preorder: [rule span children] for a rule and\n   [type text span synthetic?] for a token. The child edges and the synthetic\n   flags are part of the shape, so a tree that differs only in them differs.\"\n  [pk]\n  (mapv (fn [n]\n          (if (= :rule (:kind n))\n            [(:rule n) (:span n) (:children n)]\n            [(:type n) (:text n) (:span n) (boolean (:synthetic n))]))\n        (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))\n\n\n(defn check-ok\n  \"`source` parses to an ok packet that validates and conforms (invariants\n   1-5); with `expected` the packet's shape equals it. Returns the packet.\"\n  ([parse source] (check-ok parse source nil))\n  ([parse source expected]\n   (let [pk (parse source)]\n     (is (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk)) source)\n     (is (some? (packet/validate! pk {:source source})) source)\n     (is (= [] (packet/conform pk source)) source)\n     (when expected\n       (is (= expected (shape pk)) source))\n     pk)))\n\n\n(defn check-error\n  \"`source` yields a syntax-error packet with no nodes that validates and\n   whose first error has the given `line`, `column` and `span` (invariant 6).\n   ANTLR's line and column and the byte span are independent coordinates, so\n   each is pinned on its own. Returns the packet.\"\n  [parse source {:keys [line column span]}]\n  (let [pk (parse source)\n        e (first (:yang.cst/errors pk))]\n    (testing source\n      (is (= :yang.cst/syntax-error (:yang.cst/outcome pk)))\n      (is (not (contains? pk :yang.cst/nodes)) \"never a partial program\")\n      (is (not (contains? pk :yang.cst/root)))\n      (is (true? (:yang.cst/complete pk)))\n      (is (= :syntax-error (:kind e)))\n      (is (string? (:message e)))\n      (is (some? (packet/validate! pk {:source source})))\n      (is (= [] (packet/conform pk source)))\n      (when line (is (= line (:line e))))\n      (when column (is (= column (:column e))))\n      (when span (is (= span (:span e)))))\n    pk))\n\n\n(defn check-fixtures\n  \"Run each fixture {:source s :shape [...]} or {:source s :error {...}}.\"\n  [parse fixtures]\n  (doseq [{:keys [source shape error]} fixtures]\n    (if error\n      (check-error parse source error)\n      (check-ok parse source shape))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The adversarial corpus: packets that must be rejected\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- first-node\n  [pk pred]\n  (first (filter pred (:yang.cst/nodes pk))))\n\n\n(defn- token-of\n  [pk type]\n  (first-node pk #(and (= :token (:kind %)) (= type (:type %)))))\n\n\n(defn- edit\n  [pk id f]\n  (update-in pk [:yang.cst/nodes id] f))\n\n\n(def mutations\n  \"Named mutations of a good packet for a source with a multi-byte string\n   token; each yields a packet `validate!` and `conform` must refuse. Pair\n   with `check-mutations`.\"\n  [[\"duplicate child edge\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [r (first-node pk #(and (= :rule (:kind %)) (seq (:children %))))]\n        (edit pk (:id r) #(update % :children (fn [k] (into [(first k)] k))))))]\n   [\"wrong token text\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk (:id (token-of pk \"NAME\")) #(assoc % :text \"wrong\")))]\n   [\"collapsed synthetic NAME\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"NAME\")\n            a (first (:span t))]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :synthetic true, :text \"\", :span [a a]))))]\n   [\"span ending inside a multi-byte character\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (first-node pk #(and (= :token (:kind %))\n                                   (= \"STRING\" (:type %))))\n            a (first (:span t))]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :span [a (+ a 2)]))))]\n   [\"children out of preorder\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [r (first-node pk #(and (= :rule (:kind %))\n                                   (< 1 (count (:children %)))))]\n        (edit pk (:id r) #(update % :children (comp vec reverse)))))]\n   [\"node unreachable from the root\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [end (count (:yang.cst/nodes pk))]\n        (update pk :yang.cst/nodes conj\n                {:id end, :kind :token, :type \"NAME\", :text \"\", :span [0 0]})))]\n   [\"span past the end of the source\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk (:id (token-of pk \"NAME\")) #(assoc % :span [0 99])))]\n   [\"blank grammar name\" (fn [pk] (assoc pk :yang.cst/grammar \"\"))]\n   [\"rule name outside the grammar\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk 0 #(assoc % :rule \"no_such_rule\")))]\n   [\"real token overlapping the previous one\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"ASSIGN\")]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :span [0 (second (:span %))]))))]\n   [\"rule span not covering its children\"\n    (fn [pk] (edit pk 0 #(assoc % :span [0 1])))]\n   [\"error packet that still carries nodes\"\n    (fn [pk] (assoc pk :yang.cst/outcome :yang.cst/syntax-error))]\n   [\"EOF presented as real source\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"EOF\")]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(dissoc % :synthetic))))]\n   [\"synthetic NEWLINE in the middle of the source\"\n    (fn [pk]\n      (let [t (token-of pk \"NEWLINE\")\n            a (first (:span t))]\n        (edit pk (:id t) #(assoc % :synthetic true, :span [a a]))))]])\n\n\n(defn- refused?\n  [pk opts]\n  (try (packet/validate! pk opts)\n       false\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object\n                 :clj clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo\n                 :cljs ExceptionInfo)\n              _\n         true)))\n\n\n(defn check-mutations\n  \"`source` parses to a packet that conforms; every mutation of it is then\n   refused by both `validate!` (with the source) and `conform`.\"\n  [parse source]\n  (let [pk (parse source)\n        opts {:source source,\n              :rule-names (set (keep :rule (:yang.cst/nodes pk)))}]\n    (is (= [] (packet/violations pk opts)) \"the unmutated packet conforms\")\n    (doseq [[label f] mutations\n            :let [m (f pk)]]\n      (testing label\n        (is (not= pk m) \"the mutation changed the packet\")\n        (is (seq (packet/violations m opts)))\n        (is (seq (packet/conform m source (select-keys opts [:rule-names]))))\n        (is (refused? m opts))))))\n            (note! (:id n) :empty-rule-not-zero-width)))\n        @bad))))\n\n\n(defn violations\n  \"Every way `packet` breaks the contract, as a vector of\n   {:violation kw ...} (empty when it conforms). The structure is checked\n   first; the source-dependent checks run only on a well-formed packet and\n   only when `:source` is given. `opts`: `:source` the sealed source text,\n   `:rule-names` the grammar's rule-name set.\"\n  [packet {:keys [source rule-names]}]\n  (let [structural (structure-violations packet rule-names)]\n    (if (or (seq structural) (nil? source))\n      structural\n      (source-violations packet source))))\n\n\n(defn validate!\n  \"Return the packet when it keeps the contract (`violations`); otherwise\n   throw a qualified malformed-cst error carrying the first violation and\n   all of them. Without `opts` the check is structural; with `:source` it is\n   source-aware.\"\n  ([packet] (validate! packet nil))\n  ([packet opts]\n   (let [bad (violations packet opts)]\n     (when (seq bad)\n       (malformed! (str \"CST packet violates its contract: \"\n                        (name (:violation (first bad))))\n                   (assoc (select-keys (first bad) [:id :error])\n                          :violations bad)))\n     packet)))\n\n\n(defn node\n  [packet id]\n  (nth (:yang.cst/nodes packet) id))\n\n\n(defn root\n  [packet]\n  (node packet (:yang.cst/root packet)))\n\n\n(defn children\n  [packet n]\n  (mapv #(node packet %) (:children n)))\n\n\n(defn rule?\n  ([n] (= :rule (:kind n)))\n  ([n rule-name] (and (= :rule (:kind n)) (= rule-name (:rule n)))))\n\n\n(defn token?\n  ([n] (= :token (:kind n)))\n  ([n text] (and (= :token (:kind n)) (= text (:text n)))))\n\n\n(defn child-rules\n  \"The rule children of `n` named `rule-name`, in order.\"\n  [packet n rule-name]\n  (filterv #(rule? % rule-name) (children packet n)))\n\n\n(defn has-token?\n  [packet n text]\n  (boolean (some #(token? % text) (children packet n))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Conformance, the per-target oracle\ncollab/1792360000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:19:2. **P1 — Synthetic-token handling repeats the rejected policy.** [export.cljc:55](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-antlr-multi/src/cljc/yang/antlr/export.cljc:55) marks any text mismatch or overlap synthetic and preserves runtime text. There is no type-keyed `:synthetic-policy` or canonical helper text. A collapsed synthetic NAME passes validation and conformance. Implement the approved DEDENT/NEWLINE/EOF policy and canonical text while retaining independent exporter evidence.\ncollab/1792360000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-gate.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:21:3. **P1 — The required adversarial conformance corpus is missing.** [conformance.cljc:12](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-antlr-multi/test/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc:12) drops child edges and synthetic flags from its comparison shape; its error helper never checks columns. The exporter tests lack the twelve required mutations and the two pinned helper-token error-coordinate disagreements. The `[4 99]` mutation proves Dart executes that span assertion; it does not establish the approved oracle. Add the complete acceptance/mutation corpus on all three hosts.\ncollab/1792400000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-regate.prompt.md:25:2. P1-2 the synthetic policy: packet/synthetic-policy keyed on token type (DEDENT/EOF always synthetic;\ncollab/1792400000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-regate.prompt.md:26:   NEWLINE only at end-of-source; others never); canonical text (DEDENT \"\", NEWLINE \"\\n\", EOF \"<EOF>\");\ncollab/1792400000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-regate.prompt.md:27:   zero-width spans; the exporter decides by type with independent evidence retained. Is this the\ncollab/1792400000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-regate.prompt.md:30:   columns + the error packet; 14 mutations (the required twelve + a real EOF + a mid-file synthetic\ncollab/1792400000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-regate.prompt.md:31:   NEWLINE), each refused by BOTH validate! and conform, running on all three hosts; the two\ncollab/1792400000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-regate.prompt.md:32:   helper-token error-coordinate disagreement pins; the golden asserts children + flags.\ncollab/1792400000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-m012-regate.prompt.md:33:4. P2: §4.6 now documents the three JS compatibility additions + the per-host error-coordinate pinning;\ncollab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:26:- The JS and Dart lexer bases carry the same NEWLINE/DEDENT `commonToken`\ncollab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:184:  JS and Dart ports replace `commonToken(NEWLINE, text)`/`DEDENT` construction\ncollab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:242:   no nodes; EOF/DEDENT synthetic and zero-width. `cst_export_test.clj` becomes\ncollab/1792289000000-architect-antlr-multi-plan.claude-cloud-fable.findings.md:364:  may lag the grammar (method names, token constants `TOKEN_NEWLINE`). Bounded:\ncollab/1792304000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-plan-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:4:The revised policy accepts the zero-width DEDENT and rejects a collapsed NAME by type. The error contract also explicitly permits listener coordinates to disagree with the source span, and both helper-token error cases are pinned in the corpus. I’m checking the mutation table and retained exporter for inconsistencies.\ncollab/1792304000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-plan-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:15:- **Synthetic tokens:** the type-keyed policy accepts DEDENT `{:text \"\" :span [16 16] :synthetic true}` and rejects collapsed NAME tokens. Exporter evidence remains independent; canonical text removes runtime fallback text from packets. Three acceptance fixtures and twelve mutations are required on every host.\ncollab/1792304000000-reviewer-antlr-multi-plan-r3.gpt-6.1-sol.findings.md:16:- **Error coordinates:** source spans and verbatim ANTLR coordinates have separate invariants. JVM probes confirmed NEWLINE `{:line 3 :column 0 :span [13 14]}` and DEDENT `{:line 3 :column 0 :span [26 26]}`; both disagreements are pinned as expected values.\ncollab/1792370000000-engineer-antlr-multi-m012d.prompt.md:15:   synthetic-token policy, strict preorder checks, the adversarial corpus, the error-coordinate\ncollab/1792370000000-engineer-antlr-multi-m012d.prompt.md:16:   disagreements. The DESIGN IS THE AUTHORITY — implement to it; do NOT weaken the design to match\ncollab/1792370000000-engineer-antlr-multi-m012d.prompt.md:30:  inference with the approved type-keyed policy (DEDENT/NEWLINE/EOF and whatever 4.6 names) with\ncollab/1792370000000-engineer-antlr-multi-m012d.prompt.md:31:  canonical helper text, retaining independent exporter evidence. A collapsed synthetic NAME must\ncollab/1792370000000-engineer-antlr-multi-m012d.prompt.md:36:  columns; add the twelve mutations and the two pinned helper-token error-coordinate disagreements\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:109:independently composed observers.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:264:A frontend consists of four independently versioned parts:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:363:This is not namespace-load registration or mutation of a global\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:428:If a frontend separates analysis and lowering into independently driven\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:452:Four things are versioned independently and pinned together per request:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:616:and fixture independently. Retain source and binary notices, record SPDX\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:664:`:synthetic-policy` map keys synthetic justification on grammar role\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:665:(DEDENT always, NEWLINE at end, EOF always, other types never), and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:666:error packets carry two independent coordinate systems: the byte span\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:760:- Concurrent compilation of independent sealed units.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:976:transport-independent cursor serialization, which the current stream\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1138:  re-entries and never rolled back, so mutations made before a `raise`\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1493:  representation-independent form is a per-capture flag cell allocated\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1729:- Insertion is pure and host-independent, processing sites in sorted\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2454:- All four VMs on JVM, Node, and Dart VM, twelve lanes; Dart compiled to\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2465:- Mutation evidence, each mutation shown failing its detector once and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2479:source naive and under no-op hooks. The mutation evidence is in the S7\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2481:mutations (with codec-level tag-3 detection verified by S6 T4 `scalar-round-trip-test`\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:2796:- Two t